body:
Sorry I'm not familiar with the inner logic of sqlalchemy, but why is the return object in `_memoized_attr__exec_once_mutex` still `threading.Lock`?

https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/77fc8216a74e6b2d0efc6591c6c735687bd10002/lib/sqlalchemy/event/attr.py#L418-L431

I've observed getattr to `_ListenerCollection(...)._exec_once_mutex` leads to a func call to `_CompoundListener(...)._memoized_attr__exec_once_mutex`, which returns a `threading.Lock` and then deadlock my asyncio app.

I modify the return val of `_memoized_attr__exec_once_mutex` like @fantix does in https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/5581#issue-700744521
and it works on my tests. Is this modify correct?
``` py
class _CompoundListener(_InstanceLevelDispatch):
    __slots__ = "_exec_once_mutex", "_exec_once", "_exec_w_sync_once"

    def _set_asyncio(self):
        self._exec_once_mutex = AsyncAdaptedLock()

    def _memoized_attr__exec_once_mutex(self):
        return AsyncAdaptedLock()
```
